T|Rendered a real workspace at four widths and compared against the landed binary
B|COLOUR IS OFF IN ACTUAL USE. useColor now requires !Console.IsOutputRedirected. Claude Code always pipes the statusline command, so the bar emits zero ANSI escapes in its only real consumer: piping the landed binary yields 1 escape sequence, the new one yields 0. This followed AGENTS.md:84 and was a reasonable reading, but the user has decided the statusline is carved out of that rule, because its consumer renders ANSI rather than storing text.
B|PER-SEGMENT PALETTE LOST. Paint call sites fell from 18 to 2, so the whole line is painted one colour instead of each segment carrying its own. The source design's palette - repository blue, Claude orange, Codex purple - cannot survive that, and neither can the landed appearance.
Q|The width-budget logic that drops bars before telemetry is good and should be kept; restoring per-segment colour must not regress it, because Text.DisplayWidth must continue to measure the visible text rather than the escapes.
